      "body": "## gh-2097 rework — reply to the APPROVE review\n\nThanks for the APPROVE and the digest. This rework lap picked up the actionable digest items and fixed the CI flutter-tests red the PR's core change had caused. Three things:\n\n**1. The CI red (owned by this PR) — fixed.** The `Flutter app tests (shard 0/2)` leg failed on `agent_service_compaction_it_test.dart` IT-2 E4: after the gh-2097 run-start re-anchor, the loop's over-window relief could compact while the app's crash-safe persister still had the just-sent message in flight (`_persistSoon` appends unawaited). The structured engine then re-anchored the live transcript onto a session projection that lacked the newest message — the context silently lost it, the local-trim valve found nothing droppable (the newest remaining message alone busts the kept region), and the turn died on the guard error instead of being relieved. Cold/loaded schedules hit the race (the leg failed twice locally on a cold tree, passed warm — timing-dependent before the fix).\n\nFix: `AgentService._relieveOverWindow` now drains the pending persist BEFORE compacting (`await _persist()`, best effort) — the same ordering `_onAgentEnd` and the CLI's over-window funnel (`_persistMessages` before compaction) already enforce. No core code changed; the engine's re-anchor contract is untouched.\n\n**2. Digest item 1 (`test/compaction/structured_engine_test.dart:369` — new hunks not format-canonical) — fixed surgically.** The three NEW hunks the digest flagged (the `stale`/`fresh`/`fresh2` expect lines, 82–83 chars) are now wrapped to the canonical multi-line `expect(` shape. A whole-file `dart format` with the local SDK rewrites 363 lines of this file's pre-existing style (it predates the current formatter), which is outside the rework's surgical scope — so the two remaining >80-char lines (`:189`, `:285`) are main's pre-existing style and stay untouched.\n\n**3. Digest items 2 and 3 — acknowledged, not picked.** The file-local `waitUntil` hoist into `agent_cli_test_support.dart` (item 2) is the cross-file cleanup you already scoped to \"a later cleanup PR\"; the `flushDiagnosticLog()` straggler-enqueue note (item 3) stays as reviewed — theoretical behind the gh-1589 seal fence.\n\nThe lap also added the deterministic regression fixture for (1): an IT-2 test with a gated session-append FS (same decorator shape as the core's `FlakySessionFs`) that holds the newest record's append in flight across the relief — pre-fix it fails with exactly the guard error CI showed, post-fix it passes, deterministically (no timing dependence left)."
